            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0400" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/458: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-10-17T17:00:00+01:00">October 17, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 17—1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. McCoy requests me to advise you that he has received a letter from Lytton to
                    the effect that the Council will begin to discuss the report November 14th. This
                    will be followed by a meeting of the Committee of Nineteen and then the Special
                    Assembly.</p>
                <p>Lytton continues that Drummond calculates that a period of 2 months starting from
                    the middle of November will be occupied in dealing with the report and that
                    members of the Commission should be available during that period, though not
                    necessarily continuously.</p>
                <p>McCoy requests this information be given the War Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
